  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Task Force on Teachers for Education 2030</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Created in 2008, upon agreement in the Oslo Declaration, the International Task Force on Teachers for Education 2030, also called The Teachers Task Force (TTF), is a voluntary global alliance including national governments, intergovernmental organizations, international development agencies, civil society organizations, the private sector and UN agencies, working together to address the &apos;teacher gap&apos;, as well as implement and monitor target 4.c to achieve Education 2030 targets and commitments. A new strategy has been developed for the 2022-2025 period, in which the TTF will focus on knowledge production and dissemination, advocacy and national and regional policy learning.</narrative>
  </description>
